//
// PROBE: `sysinfo.version` and its alias `version` — the interpreter's own
// version string.
//
// The reference pushes `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")` of the `bund` crate
// (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/sysinfo/host.rs:9-12), registered as
// `sysinfo.version` with `version` as its alias
// (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/create_aliases.rs:32). Bund2 pushes
// its own crate's version instead, and reporting Bund's from Bund2 would be a
// claim rather than a preservation.
//
// So this golden is an **approved deviation** (D50): the oracle's output is
// captured as it is, and Bund2 is expected to differ from it on exactly the
// version string. The probe exists so the word is run against the oracle and
// the difference is on record rather than implied.
//
"probe: sysinfo.version pushes a version string" println
sysinfo.version type println
sysinfo.version println
"probe: version is its alias" println
version println
